{"title":"System of equations","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>system of equations</b> is a set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equations</a> which share the same <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Variable\" title=\"Variable\">variables</a>.  Below is an example of a system of equations.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef87799b3c4b6c2c9fbba2e86aae36c95bf74e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}a^2 + b^2 = 25\\\\a+b=7\\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Solve_2_variable_equations_in_less_than_5_seconds!!!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solve 2 variable equations in less than 5 seconds!!!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solving_Linear_Systems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solving Linear Systems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Gaussian_Elimination\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Gaussian Elimination</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Substitution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Substitution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Graphing\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Graphing</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Advanced_Methods\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Advanced Methods</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Convenient_Systems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Convenient Systems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Symmetry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Symmetry</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Clever_Substitution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Clever Substitution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"Solve_2_variable_equations_in_less_than_5_seconds.21.21.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solve_2_variable_equations_in_less_than_5_seconds!!!\">Solve 2 variable equations in less than 5 seconds!!!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solve 2 variable equations in less than 5 seconds!!!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Video Link: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pSYT95hSH6M\">https://youtu.be/pSYT95hSH6M</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solving_Linear_Systems\">Solving Linear Systems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solving Linear Systems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A system of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Linear\" title=\"Linear\">linear</a> equations is where all of the variables are to the power 1.  There are three elementary ways to solve a system of linear equations.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gaussian_Elimination\">Gaussian Elimination</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Gaussian Elimination\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gauss\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Gauss\">Gaussian</a> elimination involves eliminating variables from the system by adding constant multiples of two or more of the equations together.  Let's look at an example:\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Find the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> for which\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89cc5edaba92c28acdd060844345c54e35cf521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x-12y=2\\\\3x+6y=6\\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>We can eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by adding twice the second equation to the first:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin: 1em auto 1em auto\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61f8a94973835fc961b2404303aa9ac1a4df7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 12y= 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/c/d7ca36cb557594a9e40976b6be8a8c060eb5f3dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+2($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/f/98fbd83b44b3fbfe71775b8dac3381c705050c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 6y = 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef3484dea47e4fe1b08c9927c500d315668518c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{7x + 0=14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.  We can then plug in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in either of the equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553884e92b2fad72d2817a1f33f3d4f5270222d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (2)-12y &amp;= 2 \\\\ y &amp;= 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"104\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the solution to the system is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c67f1e6c098104b1cb8f1cdd6bb16f689ac3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Substitution\">Substitution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Substitution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Substitution\" title=\"Substitution\">Substitution</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The second method, substitution, requires solving for a variable and then plugging that variable into another equation therefore reducing the number of variables.  We'll show how to solve the same problem from the elimination section using substitution.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Find the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> for which\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89cc5edaba92c28acdd060844345c54e35cf521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x-12y=2\\\\3x+6y=6\\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4><p>\nThe first equation can be solved for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:  </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e382f80fc5f08fc73b99ef90c783fa5279704289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 12y + 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /></center><p>\nPlugging this into the second equation yields </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791ff9e2e05f5ec7cd719e515a8ebf06a15c292c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(12y + 2) + 6y = 6 \\Leftrightarrow 42 y = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"249\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />.  Plugging this into either of the equations and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Graphing\">Graphing</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Graphing\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The third method for solving a system of linear equations is to graph them in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane\" title=\"Plane\">plane</a> and observe where they intersect.  We'll go back to our same example to illustrate this.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Find the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> for which\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89cc5edaba92c28acdd060844345c54e35cf521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x-12y=2\\\\3x+6y=6\\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4><p>\nWe graph the two lines as follows: </p><center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Twolineintersect.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/6e/Twolineintersect.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"323\" height=\"180\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<p>From the graph, we can see that the solution to the system is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c67f1e6c098104b1cb8f1cdd6bb16f689ac3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Advanced_Methods\">Advanced Methods</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Advanced Methods\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Matrix\" title=\"Matrix\"> Matrices</a> can also be used to solve systems of linear equations.  In fact, they provide a way to make much broader statements about systems of linear equations.\n</p><p>There is a whole field of mathematics devoted to the study of linear equations called <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Linear_algebra\" title=\"Linear algebra\">linear algebra</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Convenient_Systems\">Convenient Systems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Convenient Systems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Some systems can be solved by taking advantage of specific forms.  Such systems can often seem tough to solve at first, however.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Symmetry\">Symmetry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Symmetry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the below system.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d9289246bf80332072af6b562fc22398e1fe1c02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}a+b+c+d=4\\\\a+b+c+e=8\\\\a+b+d+e=12\\\\a+c+d+e=16\\\\b+c+d+e=20\\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"96\" />\n</p><p>\nThe key here is to take advantage of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetry\" title=\"Symmetry\">symmetry</a>.  If we add up all 5 equations we will have a total of 4 of each variable on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=LHS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"LHS\">LHS</a>.  On the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=RHS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"RHS\">RHS</a> we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7ad5c5a4244830c9034efc8685e3a44acc40a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+8+12+16+20 = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70d7ffee6916cc002b9979ff628b37672c21af6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(a+b+c+d+e) = 60 \\Leftrightarrow a + b + c + d + e = 15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"404\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>So then subtracting the first equation from this leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> on the LHS and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d12348071279e90e3b2c3554b423f7d0b1eefad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15-4=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" /> on the RHS.  Subtracting this equation from the second equation leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the LHS and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1c291869fc938040f771cbf570d5888a662ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15-8=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> on the RHS.  And thus we continue on in this way to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787eedc0b38f2d3b6fcf1f18e2301afec5a35b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c,d,e)=(-5,-1,3,7,11).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Clever_Substitution\">Clever Substitution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Clever Substitution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the below system.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb9cde2584c012424b80fa23a9d9fe243b1f696.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x+y+3xy = 5\\\\ 2x+2y+4xy=8 \\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189e3ce6d1b3191e48b16849e0a5dcb1494f7d43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69ac76c53146aeef7c220aa653ce18b1702a6517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> to get the two-variable linear system below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/8655c1ab7085e6456481abc1ca8c169bbdb9d740.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}a+3b = 5\\\\ 2a+4b=8 \\end{array}\\right.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Solving the system results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf0953f43c76a5c79f339f9aee0fc2baac51413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.  Substituting that back results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598dc22afe2486653a8ef80602915f2b457815f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87ef2bb013143c7154fb708e9f259e40de6526d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />.  We can do another substitution by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8140699a7ed7185f15f23980248e9bf72e3b1db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> and substituting to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5bd003c8976bcb24aa4bb575d083d5007b6f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(2-x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />.  Rearranging results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b21273f7669ec30e0aa1fe7d3ee39b6cb333db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = x^2 - 2x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.  Finally, by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> back in, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234b330118777aba0bee513e3ade547ebd70d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.  Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> back satisfies the system.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2007 iTest Problems/Problem 2</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">1989 AIME Problems/Problem 8</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">1993 AIME Problems/Problem 3</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=System_of_equations&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Substitution\" title=\"Substitution\">Substitution</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081344\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 312/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 74/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 42/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8523/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.004      1 Template:Main\n100.00%   15.004      1 -total\n 46.67%    7.002      1 Template:Hatnote\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3806:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081344 and revision id 236367. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}